-- title:
--   Maximum principle on a node annulus: values lie in A
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and $M'$ nonzero with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element of $A$, such that $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ is a Henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, and every element of $A$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ to an element of $A_0$. Work in $F :=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field at level $q^2M'$ with the subgroup `levelH q M'`, regarded as an extension of $k_0$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $F/k_0$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F_0 = F$ and such that $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $F_0$ are linearly disjoint over $k_0$ in the stated finite-level form: for every $K'/k_0$ finite inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, any $K'$-linearly independent family $c$ and any family $a$ in $K'\cdot F_0$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ has all $a_i = 0$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ whose intersection with $k_0$ is $A$, which is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$. Let $\mathcal O \subseteq W_0$ be a Noetherian local subring of $F_0$ whose intersection with $k_0$ is again $A$, such that every $f \in \mathcal O$ has a non-unit difference $f - x$ with some $x \in \mathcal O \cap A$, and such that $F_0$ is the field of fractions of $\mathcal O$. Let $E_0 \ge 1$, $\pi_0 \in \mathcal O$, $c_x, c_y \in \mathcal O$, $u \in \mathcal O^\times$, and let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$-adic completion of $\mathcal O$ onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the $\mathfrak m_{A_0}$-adic completion $\hat A_0$ at the parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, with units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, subject to: $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$; $\iota$ sends elements of $A$ inside $\mathcal O$ to the corresponding constants `UVCrossingModel.const`; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$; $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ while $c_x$ does not. Let $W_x$ be a further valuation subring of $F_0$ containing $\mathcal O$, meeting $k_0$ in $A$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, with $c_x \in \mathfrak m_{W_x}$ and $c_y \notin \mathfrak m_{W_x}$. Let $R$ (over a residue extension $FSS$) and $R_x$ (over $FI$) be regular prolongations of $A$ to $F$ in the sense of `RegularProlongation` whose integer rings trace on $F_0$ to $W_0$ and to $W_x$ respectively. Let $S$ be the set of places $P$ of $F/\overline{\mathbb Q}$ dominating $\mathcal O$, i.e. those with $\mathcal O \subseteq P$'s valuation subring and with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in \mathfrak m_A$ for every non-unit $f$ of $\mathcal O$. Then for every $f \in F$ lying in the integers of $R_x$, in the integers of $R$, and in the valuation subring of every $P \in S$, one has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$ for every $P \in S$.
--
--   This is a maximum principle for the annulus attached to a node of the semistable model: a function integral at both ends of the node (the two Gauss valuations $R$, $R_x$ of the boundary circles) and regular at all places of the node tube takes values in $A$ at those places. It provides the integrality hypothesis needed by the node-annulus machinery, and is used in the construction of node centres for the Igusa end in the layered node rings at an arbitrary prime.
